comment = "system.Trace capability provider (BSDTrace)"

desc = <<EOD
The BSDTrace daemon, its tracectl(8) tool and the verified
/Capabilities/System/Trace.cap bundle.  BSDTrace publishes the
system.Trace capability: it opens DTrace on behalf of explicitly
authorized consumers and delegates a rights-limited descriptor to them
over a bounded two-hop transfer path, so tracing never requires opening
/dev/dtrace as root.

This is the DTrace broker.  Hardware execution tracing with Intel
Processor Trace is the separate bsdtrace package.
EOD
